 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "asof": "2026-09-15 12:52 UTC",
  "headline": "Two stops at the original line \u2014 and seven cents decided one of them",
  "standfirst": "PLTR stopped out Thursday on a low of 164.55 against a 164.62 stop, and BAC followed Monday at 60.39 after Brian Moynihan guided third-quarter investment banking fees down at least 10%. Both at the original line, \u2212$40.00 together. OKTA came on the same afternoon at 182.73 and closed 186.45 \u2014 your position +2.04%, the stock +11.98%, because the fill came after most of the move. Heat round-tripped 4.04R \u2192 2.05R \u2192 3.05R in one session and sits at the 3.0R cap. Underneath it: the ten-year touched 5.00% for the first time since October 2023, a Wednesday hike went above 90% priced, and Saudi Arabia shut the pipeline built to bypass Hormuz. Two of the three positions now open move on the same AI-safety story.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "The book",
    "right": "3 open \u00b7 2 closed \u00b7 heat 3.05R / 3.0R",
    "title": "Two stops at the original line, one entry the same afternoon, and heat right back where it started",
    "items": [],
    "note": "<b>PLTR and BAC both closed at their original stops</b>, PLTR on Thursday 10 September and BAC on Monday, realising <b>\u2212$40.00</b> \u2014 a clean \u22121.00R each, <b>2.0% of the account</b>."
   },
   {
    "kicker": "The wire \u00b7 your positions",
    "right": "3 names \u00b7 company news only",
    "title": "What is actually happening at the companies you own",
    "items": [],
    "note": "<b>Street:</b> Strong Buy \u00b7 62 analysts, average target <b>$422.34</b> \u2014 22.2% above the 345.71 close."
   },
   {
    "kicker": "What actually mattered",
    "right": "one session, filtered",
    "title": "The book is concentrated in a story, and two of its three names have already outrun the street",
    "items": [],
    "note": "<b>1. GOOG and OKTA both rose on Monday for the same reason</b>, and only the third name is unattached to it. They sit in different industries, so no screener and no sector check would flag this \u2014 it is concentration in a <i>narrative</i>, not a sector. The AI-safety trade arrived in a single session on an essay; it can leave the same way, and if it does two thirds of the book moves down together. There is no date on the calendar for it."
   },
   {
    "kicker": "The war \u00b7 the day",
    "right": "Brent above $105 \u00b7 pipeline shut five to six weeks",
    "title": "The pipeline built to survive a closed Hormuz was shut by drones from Iraq",
    "items": [],
    "note": "<b>Saudi Arabia suspended the East-West pipeline on 13 September</b> after a drone strike the kingdom traced to Maysan province in south-eastern Iraq, near the Iranian border. The 1,200km line normally carries <b>4\u20135m barrels a day</b> against a 7m maximum, running crude west to Yanbu on the Red Sea. It exists <i>precisely</i> to bypass the Strait of Hormuz \u2014 and Hormuz flows are already down to roughly <b>6\u20139m bpd</b> from more than a fifth of global supply in peacetime. Repairs are estimated at <b>five to six weeks</b>."
   },
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "FOMC Wednesday \u00b7 BoJ and expiry Friday",
    "title": "A decision tomorrow, then two central banks and an expiry inside three days",
    "items": [],
    "note": "<b>The Fed is tomorrow and the surprise is one-sided.</b> Above 90% priced means a hike is already in the price and a hold is not, so the larger move comes from the outcome nobody is positioned for \u2014 amplified by a dealer book that is short gamma. There is nothing to do before 2pm ET on Wednesday, and no room to do it: heat is at the cap."
   }
  ],
